<p style="color:#e00"><b>WARNING:</b> If the permit is not renewed by <b>next Wednesday (October 21)</b>, the employee will be required to exit China within 10 days. Overstay penalties include daily fines (¥500/day) and potential deportation with a 5-year re-entry ban.</p>

<h3 style="color:#003366;border-bottom:2px solid #003366;padding-bottom:4px">Renewal Requirements</h3>
<p>To renew both permits, the following documents must be submitted <b>before Friday (October 16)</b>:</p>

<ol>
<li><b>Passport bio page</b> (scanned copy, all four corners visible)</li>
<li><b>Current work permit</b> (front and back scanned)</li>
<li><b>Current residence permit</b> (visa page scanned)</li>
<li><b>New employment contract</b> (signed by both parties, with company seal)</li>
<li><b>Company business license</b> (copy with company seal)</li>
<li><b>Health examination report</b> (issued within the last 6 months)</li>
<li><b>Photo</b> (33mm × 48mm, white background, taken within the last 6 months)</li>
<li><b>Accommodation registration</b> (police registration form / hotel registration)</li>
</ol>

<h3 style="color:#003366;border-bottom:2px solid #003366;padding-bottom:4px">Submission Method</h3>
<p>All documents must be submitted through the <b>Foreigner's Work Management System</b>. Due to system maintenance, the original portal is temporarily unavailable. Please use the backup submission portal:</p>

